# Visual judgement

This project is an aesthetic pursuit. A change is good if the planet looks
better, not if a metric moved. Capture a PNG, read it, crop in on the thing
you are judging, and compare before/after. Do not finish from `stats` or
`climate` numbers. Those scripts can hint at a failure; they cannot tell you
it looks right. A number that improved while the picture got worse is a
failure.

## After a visual change

1. Capture. `bun run preview` writes **globe and equirect**. Use `globe` or
   `equirect` only when iterating on that projection. Shift the map with
   `bun run preview equirect --lon=90`. Overlays: `bun run preview plates`
   (also `crust`, `climate`).
2. Read the **compare** sheet if it exists, otherwise the latest capture.
3. Crop in when the feature is small on the full frame — a coast, a belt, a
   plate edge, a rain shadow. Whole-planet shots hide local shape.
   `bun run crop preview/equirect.png --x=800 --y=200 --w=600 --h=400`
   writes `preview/crop.png`. Then read that.
4. Judge the image, then change the code and repeat.

A failure that hits every seed looks like a bad roll if you only capture
one. Use `bun run sheet` when judging how a change reads across seeds.

| View | Read | Use when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| globe | `preview/compare.png` or `preview/planet.png` | 3D relief, lighting, land on the sphere, polar caps, mesh/camera. 2×2 of longitudes 0° / 90° / 180° / 270°. |
| equirect | `preview/equirect-compare.png` or `preview/equirect.png` | Whole-world layout, continent arrangement, wrap, climate belts, ice bands. |
| plates | `preview/plates-compare.png` / `preview/plates.png` and the equirect pair | Plate shapes, mixed land/ocean on a plate (darker = underwater), motion arrows. |

Read **both** globe and equirect after geography, climate, or colormap
changes. After plate or plate-motion changes, read **both plate captures**.
Globe hides the far side; equirect hides how it reads as a planet. History:
`preview/history/`, plus the `*-before.png` files.

Do not finish visual work from code or from a number. Do not open the
interactive app in any built-in agent browser. Leave that to the user
(`bun run dev` at `http://localhost:3000`).
